\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A self-loop with nonzero expectation}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{For a self-loop #{e}, the transformation is only conjugation.
In the [square-cell convention](fdip-006M), take one vertex, one loop
and one square whose attaching walk traverses that loop 4 times.
Use the [finite Wilson law](fdip-006O). With
#{G=\{1,\omega,\omega^2\}} and #{\omega=e^{2\pi i/3}}, use the
one-dimensional representation #{\rho(U)=U}. Then #{U_p=U^4=U},
the gauge action is trivial, and
##{\langle U\rangle_W
 =\frac{1-e^{-3\beta/2}}{1+2e^{-3\beta/2}}>0\qquad(\beta>0).}
Thus no general open-edge vanishing conclusion extends to self-loops.}
